<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Filching</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Thief (guild level 5)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre> filch &lt;item&gt; from &lt;target&gt;
</pre>
<p>The filch skill enables you to take things another living being is wearing: 
rings, necklaces, earrings, bracelets and anklets, and also whatever is worn 
about the waist or on the back. Nothing else they wear or wield can be filched, and you need a hand free to 
try. You can only filch from another player if you have both signed the book 
of blood.
</p><p>When you try to filch, your filch skill, with your dexterity and a little of 
your brain, and a roll are compared to the target's brain and a little 
dexterity (and a player's own filch skill). Fail by a little and nothing 
happens, and no one notices. Fail badly and you are caught: the target 
attacks you. A narrow success gets you the item, but the target catches you 
at it and attacks. Even if the target didn't notice, you still risk that 
bystanders see your crime.
</p><p>If you're good at filching, this is a fast way to get good jewelry, and also a
way to spend some quality time in jail. Not to mention, a horde of blood thirsty
enemies. 
</p><p>Filching is considered a crime, and few MUD'ers will help a thief in trouble.
Some will not help a thief at all. 
</p><p><br />
See Also:
